.SS "byte SystemEx\&.Numeric\&.Fast_ULong\&.IsIt ()"

.PP
Counts the number of bits set to 1 in a 64‑bit unsigned integer (ulong)\&. Uses the branchless parallel bit‑count algorithm ("Hacker's Delight"), which collapses bit groups step‑by‑step without loops\&. This method is extremely fast and predictable, making it ideal for embedded‑style systems, event groups, bitmask engines, and any performance‑critical numeric processing\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The number of bits set to 1 (range: 0–64)\&. 
